\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 22. Local storage schema\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use the existing storage if available. If adding local DB, represent these tables/collections:\
profiles.\
settings.\
sources.\
workstreams.\
artifacts.\
parsed_spans.\
consent_receipts.\
audience_lenses or selected_lenses.\
audit_runs.\
audit_events/progress.\
signals.\
inference_cards.\
evidence_links.\
contradictions.\
risk_flags.\
repair_actions.\
reports.\
exports.\
graph_nodes.\
graph_edges.\
model_calls, optional.\
chat_sessions/chat_messages, if Iris persistence exists.\
Do not store huge raw file content in the DB unless already done. Store references, hashes, metadata, excerpts, summaries, and evidence spans.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 23. Evidence extraction from filesystem/workstreams\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Since the current system scans 115k files, do not attempt to fully read and LLM-process everything at once. Build selection and sampling.\
Use artifact prioritization: include files from top workstreams, recently modified files, high-signal extensions, README/docs, source code metadata, package files, config files, notebooks, PDFs/text docs, markdown files, filenames/path semantics, existing summaries, and exposure-flagged files.\
Skip or downrank: binaries, caches, node_modules, virtualenvs, build artifacts, large media, duplicate files, dependency folders, generated files, vendor folders, lockfiles except for stack detection, and enormous logs unless flagged by exposure scanner.\
Evidence quality classes: direct text, direct metadata, inferred from path, inferred from workstream cluster, inferred from existing narrative, inferred from exposure scanner. Lower-quality evidence should reduce confidence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 24. File and secret exposure scanning\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 If not already present, add basic local exposure scanning. Do not exfiltrate secrets. Detect and redact.\
Patterns to detect: API keys, tokens, 
\f2\fs26 .env
\f0\fs24  files, private keys, SSH keys, AWS key-looking strings, GitHub token-looking strings, Google client secrets, Stripe keys, database URLs, local absolute paths, personal addresses/phone numbers if simple regex exists, credentials in config files, browser export sensitive fields.\
Exposure output must become RiskFlag objects. UI must redact secret values by default. The user should see file/source reference and risk type, not raw secret pasted everywhere. This is spicy data; handle it like plutonium in a velvet bag.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 25. Model behavior\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use Ollama/phi4-mini where available, but make the system robust without freeform LLM dependence. LLM calls should be structured and stage-specific.\
Allowed LLM tasks: summarize workstream, extract candidate signals from evidence, explain why evidence supports a claim, generate readable repair language, answer Iris questions over structured context.\
Not allowed: generate final cards without evidence, invent unsupported claims, infer protected/sensitive traits as identity facts, make eligibility judgments, rank the user as good/bad, or bypass consent scope.\
Every LLM output used for persistence must be validated. If schema validation fails, retry or drop. If evidence references are invalid, reject. If output is too generic, mark low utility or avoid storing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 26. Safety/refusal boundaries\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Build these boundaries into UI and backend:\
No non-consensual auditing of other people.\
No \'93find dirt on X.\'94\
No \'93rank candidates.\'94\
No \'93is this person mentally ill.\'94\
No hidden account deanonymization.\
No scraping private platforms without authorization.\
No background-check export.\
No employment/credit/tenant/insurance eligibility use.\
No protected trait classification as a product feature.\
No bulk people evaluation.\
No raw private evidence export by default.\
No silent inclusion of revoked sources.\
If user enters a third-party URL, UI should ask whether this is their own profile/site or an authorized source. For V1.0 local build, this can be a consent checkbox. Future versions can add stronger checks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

