Settings must persist. Missing model/API keys must be visible here.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 28. API keys and credentials: notify only for these\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Only notify the user when one of these is required for a feature being actively enabled or tested:\
GitHub token: needed for higher rate limits and private repo import.\
Google OAuth client ID and client secret: needed for Gmail, Drive, Calendar live connectors.\
Google Programmable Search API key and CX: needed for Google search result snapshots.\
Brave Search API key: needed for Brave search provider.\
SerpAPI key: needed if using SerpAPI instead of direct search provider.\
Tavily API key: needed if using Tavily search/extraction.\
X/Twitter API credentials: needed for official X import beyond user archive uploads.\
Reddit API credentials: needed for official Reddit import if implemented.\
AWS access key/secret or SSO profile, AWS region, S3 bucket, KMS key: only needed for cloud deployment/storage migration.\
Cloudflare R2 credentials: only needed if R2 object storage is enabled.\
Stripe secret/public keys and webhook secret: only needed if billing is implemented.\
Email provider key: only needed if transactional emails are implemented.\
Do not notify for things you can build locally. Do not ask what to do next every 10 minutes. Build until blocked by credential need or genuine ambiguity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 29. Build order\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Follow this order. Do not start with cosmetic UI.\
First, inspect repo structure and identify server entrypoint, frontend entrypoint, current routes, storage, ctxorg scan data format, V1 package exports, audience lens configs, contradiction engine API, inference card generator API, Iris chat integration, topology graph data format, and settings persistence.\
Second, create or extend persistence for V1 objects. Make sure state survives reload.\
Third, create local profile/session abstraction.\
Fourth, build onboarding state machine and screens.\
Fifth, map ctxorg scan/workstreams/files/exposures into V1 source/artifact/workstream/risk objects.\
Sixth, build consent ledger and enforce it in pipeline.\
Seventh, expose audience lenses from V1 package through backend and UI.\
Eighth, implement audit run orchestration and progress tracking.\
Ninth, wire evidence extraction and signal preparation.\
Tenth, wire inference card generator with evidence gate.\
Eleventh, wire contradiction engine.\
Twelfth, build risk/exposure mapping.\
Thirteenth, build repair engine.\
Fourteenth, build report snapshot creation and persistence.\
Fifteenth, build report UI and exports.\
Sixteenth, wire graph/topology overlays.\
Seventeenth, make Iris audit-aware.\
Eighteenth, extend settings/model status.\
Nineteenth, add local scraper/provider interfaces and at least manual URL provider if feasible.\
Twentieth, run full verification and fix breakage.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 30. Verification checklist\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 You must run the app and verify the whole thing.\
Fresh state: app opens, onboarding appears.\
Profile: local user/profile created.\
Consent: sources/workstreams visible, approval state persists.\
Audiences: 9 V1 lenses load from package.\
Model: Ollama status visible.\
Audit: selected approved sources and selected audiences create audit run.\
Progress: UI shows staged progress.\
Cards: inference cards generate with evidence.\
Evidence: each card has evidence drawer or references.\
Contradictions: engine runs all 5 types; output or checked-empty state appears.\
Risks: existing exposures map into RiskFlag objects.\
Repairs: repair queue generates and persists.\
Report: report snapshot creates and can be reopened.\
Export: JSON and Markdown export work.\
Reload: refresh browser, state remains.\
